# SfxLab family v2: layer id name type dur seed key=value... (dur 0 = endless) · range id param lo hi [note] · bind signal id|* param [lo hi] [rel] [steps=N | scale=<chord>] · note text · then `spell <id>` sections: name, recipe, the spell's layers at their lock values, its binds and notes
bench 1
root 65.4064
# pyretic v3 — the searching mix, voiced by register and by chord tone, arm-agnostic. One bass bed at C2 and nothing else
# below C3. Four voices at C3-C4, one per chord tone of the harmonic series (root, third, fifth, seventh), each brought in by
# its tone.* signal: however the motions are spread over the arms, a ratio near 2/4/8 sings the root, near 3/6 the fifth,
# near 5 the third, near 7 the seventh, and a ratio gliding between integers walks through them. The cloud is the chord that
# forms: it grows with the number of motions (stack), stays a soft cluster while the ratios are detuned and gathers once every
# engaged ratio is an integer (coherence). The orb colours everything: its swing opens the voices' low-pass, its curl makes
# the fifth shimmer and steers the third's phaser notches, its speed steers the root's. fit (the reach hint) steadies the notes: a wrong reach
# leaves the root and third wobbling, the right one lets them ring clean.
