range bed level 0.08 0.35 rests at 0.35, steps back to 0.2 once the arms move and a further 0.12 as the machine fills (stack); no echo or reverb on the bass
range third level 0 0.4 the third: synth8 down to E4
range root level 0 0.22 the root: synth12 up two octaves to C4 (at C3 its partials still carried sub-bass)
range fifth level 0 0.15 the fifth: an additive tone at G4, brighter with tension
range fifth bank 0.2 0.8 harmonic richness
range seventh level 0 0.12 the seventh: a darker tone at Bb4
range cloud level 0 0.3 the chord, growing with the number of motions; spells raise it and pick the chord
range cloud gather 0.5 1 a soft cluster while searching, the chord once every ratio is an integer
range fire level 0 0.5 the near-miss flicker: rises with the pinned spell's score
bind stir bed level 0.35 0.2
bind stack bed level 0 -0.12 rel
bind orb.accel bed drive 0 0.03
bind tone.root root level 0 0.22
bind tone.third third level 0 0.4
bind tone.fifth fifth level 0 0.15
bind tone.seventh seventh level 0 0.12
bind tension fifth bank 0.2 0.8
bind stack cloud level 0 0.3
bind coherence cloud gather 0.5 1
bind radiance cloud reverb 0.3 0.7
bind fit root shimmer 0.3 0
bind fit third shimmer 0.3 0
bind orb.radius root cutoff 0.3 0.9
bind orb.radius third cutoff 0.3 1
bind orb.radius fifth cutoff 0.35 0.9
bind orb.radius seventh cutoff 0.3 0.8
bind orb.curl fifth bank_shimmer 0 0.6
bind orb.curl third ph_pos 0 1
bind orb.speed root ph_pos 0 1
bind score fire level 0 0.5
note v3 register plan. Below C3 there is only the bed (synth1 at C2). The notes are chord tones, not arms: root = synth12 at
note C4, third = synth8 at E4, fifth = a sine-plus-bank tone at G4, seventh = a darker tone at Bb4. Each is brought in by its
note tone.* signal (the reach sitting on that pitch class, from any arm), so the mix is arm-agnostic like the tuning itself.
note cloud: level with stack (one motion = a whisper, six = the chord), gather with coherence (detuned = soft cluster,
note integers = chord), reverb with radiance (Z). The orb's radius opens every voice's low-pass (wide swing = bright, tight
note = dark), its curl shimmers the fifth and steers the third's phaser, its speed steers the root's (ph pos: the orb parks the notches). fit steadies the root and third.
note fire: the pinned spell's score is its level (the near-miss flicker). Textures per spell live in the spell files, low-passed.
note Spells do not set the voices; they set the bed, the cloud's chord, their textures and one-shots.

